WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.187
The decisions.

2
00:00:01.187 --> 00:00:04.638
Who owns each namespace,
the Grid or a cloud.

3
00:00:04.638 --> 00:00:08.938
Which middleware platform, and so which
network and resolver path it uses.

4
00:00:08.938 --> 00:00:10.900
The hub design in each cloud.

5
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:14.314
And whether Oracle's private
access is needed at all,

6
00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:16.775
remembering that it's routing, not DNS.

7
00:00:16.775 --> 00:00:19.250
The next steps are the
things I couldn't verify.

8
00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:25.075
Which Oracle environment and hostnames
the agency's Core HCM tenant will use.

9
00:00:25.075 --> 00:00:29.086
Whether API-driven inbound
provisioning is available in the U.S.

10
00:00:29.086 --> 00:00:30.600
Government Graph cloud.

11
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:34.741
Whether Azure's DNS Private
Resolver, Lifecycle Workflows and

12
00:00:34.741 --> 00:00:39.200
Connect private endpoints are
available in the government clouds.

13
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.567
And the VMware install
guides' DNS rules and Oracle's

14
00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:45.700
own connectivity patterns,
which I couldn't open.

15
00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:47.375
They're all listed in the backup.

16
00:00:47.375 --> 00:00:48.512
Where does this fit?

17
00:00:48.512 --> 00:00:51.540
Book 03 covers HR-driven identity,

18
00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:58.351
with Federal HR 2.0 in Chapter 03 and
the provisioning pipeline in Chapter 05.

19
00:00:58.351 --> 00:01:04.987
Book 08 covers DNS, DHCP and IP address
management: split-brain DNS in Chapter 02,

20
00:01:04.987 --> 00:01:11.828
cloud private endpoints in Chapter 07,
the reference architecture in Chapter 08,

21
00:01:11.828 --> 00:01:15.300
and the migration sequence in Chapter 10.

22
00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:21.639
Three research items sit beside this one:
Trinzic Alone, or Trinzic Plus Cloud DDI;

23
00:01:21.639 --> 00:01:26.937
Infoblox DDI for Federal Agencies;
and Who Names the Device After AD.

24
00:01:26.937 --> 00:01:30.433
One note on standing: this
is research under review,

25
00:01:30.433 --> 00:01:33.263
not an endorsement by any federal agency.

26
00:01:33.263 --> 00:01:34.025
Thank you.

